Well, in keeping with the saying, what is the attraction of Lojban to you?  Why 
not take up Klingon, which has a definite culture and definitive answers to your 
haja questions (haja form the pluperfect subjunctive?, a question liable to get 
more muddy than xorlo in Lojban)?  Or toki pona, that takes about a day to learn 
enough to carry on conversations on a range of things and contribute to the 
list? And, while most of your contributions have been about haja questions or 
general learning aids (the best app for your smartphone, say), you have taken 
part in earlier rounds of the eternal xorlo issue so, are not completely 
uninterested nor ignorant.  So, what do you think {lo broda} means?





